{
	"version": 2,
	"_doc": [
		"The UI screen registry read by UiAudit.screens() / UiAudit.audit_screen(t, id) (tests/lib/ui_audit.gd): one row per screen of UI_NAVIGATION.md section 5.1 that has a scene or a fixture, plus the two P07 gallery pages.",
		"It is the SAME file as design_ui/ui_screens.proposed.json: the lead copies it as it is. The rows `language` (parts of the title and of the settings) and `sleep` (a fade in world_2d.gd) have no scene of their own: they have no row, their proofs are named checks (menus.language_switch_no_errors, zz_acceptance.sleep_and_passout_ui).",
		"A row has NO status: UiAudit derives it (pending = no scene, legacy = the old scaffold main_menu / character_select that is not on the guide theme yet, live = the scene exists). A row that is part of another screen's scene (the intro, the minimap) has no scene of its own: its `tripwire` is the file whose appearance makes it live.",
		"kind: scene | modal | hud | component | surface | fade. focus: initial | none (none = audited like a HUD: no control may take focus). modal: the GameManager modal name. esc_depth: how many Esc presses close the screen; 0 = Esc does nothing (the audit presses it once).",
		"checks: initial_focus | focus_walk | focusable_report | rule_report | text_field_audit | escape_chain | ring_pixels | panel_pixels | button_pixels | i18n_flip | mouse_walk | theme_report | compare_guide (compare_guide is the windowed python tool: info only).",
		"  escape: {vias: [key, pad_b, start]} (only for esc_depth 0 rows: the same screen is pressed three ways), {settle_seconds}, {expect_focus}, {release_world_focus}. A row with esc_depth 1 and a `modal` is proved by the audit itself; deeper chains and scene-backs by the owner's own UiAudit.escape_chain call.",
		"options (validated by UiAudit.validate_options('registry', ...): a typo fails the row): ignore [globs] | max_steps (0 = auto) | wrap + wrap_axes | via | tabs | replay | accept | consumes | expect_edges | echo | pad_check | dirs | start | pages + max_pages + tab_groups (the page behind every radio tab / chip is audited too) |",
		"  strict_typography | strict_gold | gold_source | hit_min (default 32) | same_ok | forbid_disabled_focus | forbid_windows | list_like | click | panel | button | settle_seconds.",
		"compare: informational only (tests/checkpoints/compare_guide.py is a separate windowed tool; the guide mocks show their focus-ring-free state, a MenuRow / ChoiceRow keeps its gold FOCUS fill: UI_NAVIGATION.md D12).",
		"WHEN A PACKAGE LANDS A SCREEN nothing is edited here: the scene appears and the derived status becomes live; the owner calls `await UiAudit.audit_screen(t, \"<id>\")` from the section. The gold fill / ring, the walk, the rules and the Esc depth are then enforced."
	],
